# The GitHub runner image's own trees, excluded from the walk: its toolchain
# caches and the system directories the image itself makes world-writable (the
# first --deep run measured 210,280 world-writable entries, 345k of them under
# /usr/local/lib alone). No host of anyone's owns these permissions, and a path
# absent from a later image is harmless.
#
# Ruling G-26: ONE copy, read by ci.yml's collect-root job (the walk flags and
# the diagnostic find that explains a capped list) and by examples.yml's VM
# collect. The VM example is only "the walk CI already proves" while the two
# runs exclude exactly the same trees, and a second inline copy is how that
# stops being true.
#
# One absolute path per line; a line starting with # is a comment.
/opt/hostedtoolcache
/opt/pipx
/opt/runner-cache
/opt/microsoft
/opt/az
/imagegeneration
/usr/share
/usr/local/lib
/usr/local/share
/usr/local/.ghcup
/usr/lib/jvm
